### Dana's client refreshes: RFC 6749 §6, and the refresh token rotates (RFC 9700 §4.14)
# @name DanaRefreshes
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={{DanaRefresh}}

### A second tab sends the same, now-rotated token at once — inside the grace window, it gets the same child
# @name DanaReplaysInsideWindow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={{DanaRefresh}}

### The same rotated token after the window is reuse. Polled — never slept — until the window (10 s) has passed;
### a replay still inside it answers the same child again, so the poll cannot fork the family. At most ~30 s.
# @name ReuseAfterWindow
## RETRY-UNTIL-TEST-PASS: The rotated token, replayed after the grace window, is refused as invalid_grant.
## RETRY-MAX-ATTEMPTS: 30
## RETRY-BACKOFF-TYPE: Constant
## RETRY-MAX-DELAY: 00:00:01
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={{DanaRefresh}}
